<Legal title="Distance Sales Agreement" description="Distance sales agreement and pre-information for Spending Atlas Plus and Plus+ web subscriptions.">
  <p>
    This agreement covers Spending Atlas subscriptions bought through harcama-atlas.pages.dev under Turkish Consumer Protection Law No. 6502 and the Distance Contracts
    Regulation. You accept that you have read and approved this text before pressing the purchase button on the checkout page. The information provided before purchase is in
    the <a href="/en/legal/pre-information">Pre-Information Form</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Parties</h2>
  <h3>Seller (merchant of record)</h3>
  <p>
    Sales on the web are made by our authorised reseller <strong>Paddle.com Market Ltd</strong> (Judd House, 18–29 Mora Street, London EC1V 8BT, United Kingdom). Paddle takes
    the payment, issues the invoice, and Paddle’s name appears on your card statement. Paddle’s buyer terms also apply to this sale.
  </p>
  <h3>Service provider</h3>
  <p>
    <Fill k="unvan" label="Şirket unvanı" />, <Fill k="adres" label="Açık adres" />, MERSIS: <Fill k="mersis" label="MERSİS no" />, Tax office and no:
    <Fill k="vergiDairesi" label="Vergi dairesi" /> / <Fill k="vergiNo" label="Vergi no" />, Phone: <Fill k="telefon" label="Telefon" />, Email:
    <Fill k="eposta" label="E-posta" />, KEP: <Fill k="kep" label="KEP adresi" />.
  </p>
  <h3>Buyer</h3>
  <p>The person signed in with a Spending Atlas account at the time of purchase who enters their details on the checkout page.</p>

  <h2>2. Subject</h2>
  <p>
    The subject of this agreement is the provision of the Spending Atlas Plus or Plus+ plan chosen by the Buyer as a digital service for the chosen period (monthly or yearly).
    Plan features are listed on the <a href="/en/pricing">Pricing</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Price and payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The price, including taxes, is shown on the checkout page before purchase. If a promo code is used, the discounted amount appears in the same place.</li>
    <li>Payment is taken by credit or debit card through Paddle. Card details never reach the Service provider.</li>
    <li>The subscription renews automatically at the same price at the end of the chosen period until cancelled. If the price changes, you are informed before renewal.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Free trial</h2>
  <p>
    Plus and Plus+ can be tried free for 7 days by first-time subscribers. Nothing is charged during the trial; if you cancel before it ends, no payment is made. If you do not
    cancel, the first period’s fee is charged when the trial ends. Accounts that have subscribed before are not offered a trial.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Plan changes</h2>
  <p>
    When switching from Plus to Plus+, the difference between the two plans for the remaining time of the current period is charged immediately; the amount is shown before you
    confirm. Moving to a lower plan or changing the period is calculated the same way.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Performance</h2>
  <p>The service is activated on the Buyer’s account right after payment is confirmed (or the trial starts) and can be used with the same account on the web, iOS and Android apps.</p>

  <h2>7. Right of withdrawal</h2>
  <p>
    The Buyer may withdraw within 14 days of the contract date without giving a reason. The notice can be sent to <Fill k="eposta" label="E-posta" /> or via the link in Paddle’s
    invoice email. On withdrawal, the amount paid is refunded to the card used within 14 days of the notice at the latest. Details are on the
    <a href="/en/legal/cancellation-refund">Cancellation and Refunds</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Cancellation</h2>
  <p>
    The Buyer can cancel the subscription at any time on the <a href="/en/account/subscription">My subscription</a> page. Cancellation takes effect at the end of the period; plan
    features remain available until then and nothing is charged for the next period.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Disputes</h2>
  <p>
    The Buyer may submit complaints and objections to the consumer arbitration committee of their place of residence or of the place of the transaction, within the monetary
    limits set yearly by the Ministry of Trade, and to the consumer court for disputes above those limits.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Entry into force</h2>
  <p>By confirming the purchase on the checkout page, the Buyer is deemed to have accepted all terms of this agreement. A copy of the agreement is always available on this page.</p>
</Legal>
